<<~ ahu #/the-record-laws>>

!! The record laws ~ what a command IS, and where a name lives

Two laws the door has always obeyed and no carrier has stated.

!!! Records, not RPC

''A command rides as an intent RECORD; an outcome rides as a receipt RECORD.'' Neither reads as a remote
call. Each record flows through the admin surface as a ''local-first artifact'' — authored, addressed,
and readable after the fact by anything that can read a tiddler. A temporary record stays acceptable where
the flow needs only a short life; a call that leaves no record does not.

''What the law buys:'' an RPC leaves a trace only where someone logged one, and the log answers to a
different grammar than the call. A record IS the trace, in the grammar everything else already reads.

!!! The `lar:` locality law

''Every system `id` uses the `lar:` URI scheme'' — command ids, receipt ids, audience ids, principal ids,
session artifact ids, storage artifact ids, and any other first-class name.

''The authority says where the named thing lives:''

<<~ scale locality """hostless ~ "`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/commands/promote/…`" — a hot, warm or cold STORAGE artifact, on-disk projections first -> hostful ~ "`lar://node.alpha.local/ha.ka.ba/bags/sessions/live/…`" — a LIVE session artifact, named at the node holding it""">>

''So one glance at a name says whether the thing it names outlives the session.'' A hostless name outlives
the node; a hostful one does not, and reading a hostful name as durable NAMES the failure this law makes
visible.

''Provenance:'' harvested verbatim from `lar:///lares_research/research-streams/lararium/LARES-CLI-DAEMON-SPRINT-PLAN`,
where both laws stood settled with no live carrier holding either.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-law>>

! The Vessel Door ~ a substrate collapse

''ONE NAMESPACE PER CAUSAL ISLAND; THE PLANE IS A PARAMETER, NEVER A NEW VERB.'' That law already governs
this CLI. It collapsed the sensorium surface to two doors — one sovereign, one guest — folding ten
top-level verbs away with no legacy aliases kept.

''The vessel is a causal island and speaks through ONE name.'' Its store, its genesis artifact, its
daemon and its corpus form one island by every test this house applies, so they answer at one door. ''A
plane with no door has nowhere to put new capability but the top level'' — which is why the verb count
grows back wherever the law has not reached, and where to look when it does.

''This meme carried the work order, and the work stands done.'' The reasoning lives elsewhere; what follows records what the collapse enacted, so a reader meets the shape rather than re-deriving it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-primitives>>

!! What the door answers — SEVEN primitives

Every substrate motion in this CLI composes from these, and no composition earns a primitive's seat.

<<~ has Primitive stop "ends a running daemon by port, graceful then forced ~ never a restart in disguise">>
<<~ has Primitive wipe "pares the vessel store + the projection watermark ~ identity, seal, library and registry stand outside it">>
<<~ has Primitive build "compiles the workspace and STAMPS the source digest ~ a build that skips the stamp leaves the tree reading stale">>
<<~ has Primitive bake "re-derives the genesis island from the engine + the packed plugin ~ moves NO identity">>
<<~ has Primitive found "mints the vessel identity, the persona root, the social planes and the bootstrap ~ idempotent, skips what stands">>
<<~ has Primitive stand "brings the daemon up, foreground or detached, and reports what it found ~ attach when one already answers">>
<<~ has Primitive seed "plants every bags holding back into its doc, kind-routed, diff-gated ~ idempotent; a converged tree no-ops">>

''An eighth reads, and belongs beside them'': `read` — the pure inspection that starts nothing (bootstrap
presence, storage size, port, seal state, personas, quorum).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-collapse>>

!! The collapse, verb by verb

Each row names a RETIRED spelling and the composition that carries it now. ''No aliases survive'' — a name
that still answers teaches that both spellings stand, and the surface regrows from there. Every spelling
below refuses with `unknown command`, flags included: routing an unknown name to the global help would
return 0 and print a full page, which reads exactly like a door that opened.

|! retired |! composes |! answers at |
| `init` | found | `vessel found` |
| `wake` | found? · stand · read | `vessel stand` (the entry point; keeps its report) |
| `serve` | stand (foreground) | `vessel stand --foreground` |
| `dev` | stand · vite | `vessel stand --with-app` |
| `stop` | stop | `vessel stop` |
| `reset` | wipe · found | `vessel clear` |
| `fresh` | wipe · stand | `vessel clear && vessel stand` |
| `reconcile` | stop · wipe? · stand | `vessel stand --restart [--clear]` |
| `refresh` | build · stop · wipe · stand | `vessel rite refresh` |
| `rebuild` | bake · stand | `vessel rite rebuild` |
| `build-genesis` | bake | `vessel bake` |
| `regenesis` | stop · wipe · bake · stand · seed | `vessel rite rebirth` |
| `seed` | seed | `vessel seed` |
| `status` · `node status` | read | `vessel read` |

''THE COMPOSITIONS RIDE AS RITES, NEVER VERBS.'' `refresh`, `rebuild` and `rebirth` are pet-named
cap-stacks over the primitives, and this house already carries the surface for exactly that: a rite-door
where new capability arrives as a new rite rather than another raw verb. A composition earns a pet-name;
it never earns a top-level name.

''The test for a rite versus a primitive'': a primitive names one motion
and cannot be expressed as a sequence of the others. Everything else composes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-founding-rite>>

!! ⚠ The founding rite rides the rite-door, and one movement changes

''The founding rite composes: found · stand · seed.'' No stop, no wipe, no second bake — a fifth movement
that stopped the daemon, wiped the store and re-baked genesis would tear down what the second movement
built ninety seconds earlier. The only part a founding needs there is the seeding.

''AND THAT SUBTRACTION REMOVES A TRAP RATHER THAN HIDING IT.'' Sealing the vault writes a marker the clear
does not remove, so every later daemon boot wants the passphrase in its environment. A movement that
RESTARTS the daemon crosses that gate — and an operator who sealed by typing would carry the passphrase
forward by hand between two movements or watch the vessel come up at the floor. ''A rite that never
restarts never crosses the gate'', so no carry-forward step exists to get wrong.

''`rebirth` stands as its own rite.'' Rebirth of a STANDING vessel names a real motion and stop-wipe-bake
carries it exactly. It simply never serves as a founding step, and its name says so.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-ripples>>

!! Every caller that must close with the collapse

''A collapse that leaves callers on old names has not collapsed anything.'' These surfaces name substrate
verbs directly, so each MUST move in the same act — and each row below names what keeps it moved.

# ''THE GENERATED MCP MIRROR.'' The CLI↔MCP↔seat isomorphism rides a GENERATED fixture, never a
  hand-edited one. Rebuild the CLI first, then regenerate. A hand-edit here reads as a passing test over a
  surface nobody generated — and so does a fixture nobody regenerated, which is why the weld rides a
  witness (#/the-verifications) rather than a habit.
# ''THE FRESH-BUILD GATE.'' Membership DERIVES from the door rather than from a remembered list of verb
  names. A roster drifts the moment a surface changes — the very defect this door closes. The derived
  test states its EXCEPTIONS instead, so it fails safe: a sub-door added later stays gated until someone
  argues it out.
# ''THE FOUNDING RITE.'' Its preflight, its clear, its stand, its seed and its live movements all name
  substrate verbs directly. It is the operator-instruction source, so a stale command there fails at the
  worst moment a command can fail.
# ''THE KEEPER REHEARSAL HARNESS.'' It walks the rite by name. Its preflight, its per-cycle clear, its
  founding step and its seed step all move.
# ''THE CONTAINER BOOT + THE WITNESS SCRIPTS.'' They found and stand vessels by verb name.
# ''THE SESSION-START HOOK.'' It calls the entry point with the observe capability. The capability must
  survive the rename intact — a hook that gains the standing capability by accident turns looking into
  acting.
# ''EVERY HANDLER'S OWN HEADER.'' A moved handler whose docstring still self-names its old spelling is the
  cosmetic residue the previous collapse left; sweep it in the same pass rather than leaving it again.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-stands>>

!! What does NOT move, and why

''NOT the noun-doors.'' `nexus`, `persona`, `vault`, `library`, `circle`, `cabal`, `hooks`, `sense`,
`mempalace`, `sensorium` already obey the law. Touching them spends risk for nothing.

''NOT the content verbs.'' `bag`, `wiki`, `ingest`, `act`, `edge`, `draft`, `normalize`, `repack` name the
corpus island rather than the vessel island. They may want their own door one day; that is a separate
reading and it does not belong in this act.

''NOT the identity verbs.'' `device-admit` and `raise` name ceremonies between vessels, not motions of
one vessel's substrate. ''An OWED capability carries no door at all'' — the Nexus invite ceremony rides
no verb until its transport lands, the same way `cabal feed` stands built and unspelled.

''NOT the capabilities themselves.'' Nothing here adds or removes what the CLI can do. Every primitive
already runs inside a verb being collapsed; this act changes only how many names reach them.

''A collapse that also changes behaviour cannot be verified'' — a green
suite afterward would prove neither half. Move the names; move nothing else.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-verifications>>

!! What proves it landed

''Each of these fails loudly on a partial collapse'', and each now rides a witness rather than a hand —
because a verification an operator has to remember to run is a verification that reports on their memory.

# ''The tree typechecks'' — `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`. A green build has not typechecked: the compiler
  colorizes, so a reader grepping for the word `error` and its code matches nothing while a package
  carries dozens. The witness reads per package and exits non-zero on any real error.
# ''The mirror names the table the CLI carries'' — `tools/mirror-parity-witness.sh`. The generated
  isomorphism fixture goes stale by NOT being regenerated, and the checks standing around it cannot see
  that: the three-way guard asserts the fixture's own internal coherence (which staleness satisfies), and
  the projection test compares live to live. ''Nothing else welds the fixture to the table.''
# ''No old name answers'' — `tools/rite-commands-witness.sh` reads the live projection. Every collapsed
  spelling MUST fail as an unknown verb, ''with or without `--help`''. A surviving alias is the failure
  mode this collapse exists to prevent, and it hides perfectly behind a passing suite.
# ''The surface gets measured at the VERB, never at the door.'' A door count reports a collapse the
  operator cannot feel: the fan-out lives one level below the number, so a surface that reads halved by
  doors may not have moved at all. Both figures DERIVE, printed on every rite-commands run — ''the pair is
  the reading, either alone flatters'', and a figure transcribed into prose ages silently.
# ''The keeper rehearsal walks both cycles green'' — which also proves the founding rite composes
  correctly, since the harness performs the rite rather than describing it.
# ''The founding rite reads end to end'', every instructed sub-door resolving at a DISPATCH POSITION. A
  substring test reads the vocabulary of a file rather than its dispatch, and passes on the very line that
  disproves it — `case "contract": … cmdContract(args, "admit")` waved a rite instructing `nexus admit`
  straight through. A rite amended by many hands drifts fastest at exactly the commands nobody re-typed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-order>>

!! The order to work in

''Land the substrate collapse only on a quiet tree.'' It touches the entry point every other thread stands
on, so it wants to arrive between phases rather than during one.

<<~ loops "✶ primitives-and-door -> ⏿ rites -> ◇ ripples -> ▶ verifications -> ↺ the-rite-and-its-harness">>

# ''Stand the door and the primitives first, with the old verbs still answering.'' The two surfaces
  co-exist for exactly one commit, which keeps every caller working while the new shape gets proven.
# ''Move the rites'' — the compositions, pet-named through the rite surface.
# ''Close the ripples in one act'' — the generated mirror, the fresh-build gate, the rite, the harness,
  the container boot, the witnesses, the hook, the handler headers.
# ''Then cut the old names, all of them, in a single commit.'' No aliases, no deprecation window. A
  half-collapse is worse than none: it doubles the surface it was meant to halve and teaches that both
  spellings stand.
# ''Run every verification.'' A red here names a ripple that did not close, and the list above says which.

''The one-commit cut is the whole discipline.'' The previous
collapse held to it and the surface stayed collapsed; the surface that grew back is the one the law never
reached.

<<~/ahu>>

